WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.425
So, four decisions.

2
00:00:01.425 --> 00:00:04.563
Put training in every
gate, measured against a

3
00:00:04.563 --> 00:00:08.113
roster from HR and identity
records, not a headcount.

4
00:00:08.113 --> 00:00:12.326
A gate passes with a gap only
as a named, dated exception.

5
00:00:12.326 --> 00:00:14.828
Train and verify the help desk first,

6
00:00:14.828 --> 00:00:18.500
before any new role is assigned
and before every wave.

7
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:20.779
Name the owners and keep them apart:

8
00:00:20.779 --> 00:00:24.786
the chief human capital officer
and the C I O set competencies,

9
00:00:24.786 --> 00:00:30.287
the CISO owns the security words, and the
training lead reports while others decide.

10
00:00:30.287 --> 00:00:35.713
And certify with artifacts: capstones
and two credentials, renewed every year.

11
00:00:35.713 --> 00:00:37.912
The next step needs no procurement.

12
00:00:37.912 --> 00:00:40.359
Build the role roster from HR records,

13
00:00:40.359 --> 00:00:43.516
coded positions and
eligible-role assignments;

14
00:00:43.516 --> 00:00:48.645
name a training lead and an owner for each
track; and brief the workforce office,

15
00:00:48.645 --> 00:00:53.538
labor relations and the Section 508
program manager before the first gate.

16
00:00:53.538 --> 00:00:56.301
People, not tools, close the gap.

17
00:00:56.301 --> 00:01:00.025
Book 16 has the detail,
every claim footnoted.

18
00:01:00.025 --> 00:01:00.840
Thank you.
